    rules: [
      "The Overview rates a stop by the mean of its load score and the mood of the people waiting: load = waiting / (L × W × STOP_CAPACITY_PER_M2 = 2 people per m²); its score is 1 up to STOP_LOAD_EASY = 25 % and falls to 0 when full (stopLoad).",
      "Neighbours within 1.3 m; closer than the sum of their radii R (0.3 m × √space each: 0.6 m for two people of one space) they push apart with 1.4 (R − d)/R m/s; density = max(0, neighbours − 2).",
      "Walking: v = unit(target − pos) × speed × min(1, dist/0.8) / (1 + 0.12 × density) + push; standing: 0.6 (target − pos) + 0.7 push; velocity eased (4/s).",
      "Mood per s while waiting: −(0.002 + 0.005 × density + 0.006 after 60 s) plus the disruptions' mood; boarding +0.02; leaving +0.008 − 0.004 × density.",
      "Arrivals: Poisson(base_rate × demand × disruption demand × wave × L/25 × the hour's demand × dt); none while closed, out of service, or without others; at most 40 at a bus or tram stop in the street.",
      "A track of the stop closed on its own (dock closed): newcomers wait at the other tracks; those waiting for it go over to another one, or leave (0.25/s) when every track is closed.",
      "The board's next train (statusLines): the soonest timer of the tracks that are open; none while every track is closed. At a rail line's own platform the line's next trains; at a platform shared with the timetable both, the soonest first.",
      "A standing vehicle is boarded while it has more than 6 s to go (a real train always).",
      "Profiles of the others: a trip of 30 km at a station, 4 km at a bus or tram stop (their luggage); agents bring their owner's.",
      "Doors: one person after the other per vehicle and door (a door clock), the alighting first; those with an aid, a pram or bulky luggage through access_door of the vehicle type; a ramp or a lift once out serves the next wheelchair user.",
      "The doors stay open (holdUntil) while somebody is in one (at most 60 s past the dwell; a ramp or a lift in use as long as it takes), and while people wait at one for at most 20 s past it; the seconds past the dwell are counted.",
      "Load when a vehicle comes in: the riders of other simulations who stay on + onboard_share × spaces × the hour's demand × the passenger demand; a person takes their space, else as much as is left down to their least (people.everybody.squeeze_mood per space and minute of the ride, 10 min for the others), else left behind (full); a wheelchair needs a free wheelchair place.",
      "Left behind: mood −0.25, the vehicle not wanted again; the others leave after the second time.",
      "A line's bus or tram on its way need not stand out its dwell: the passengers note on it when its stop's people are looked after (seenAt) and while somebody is still getting on or off (busyAt), and it leaves once nobody is (core/transit.js).",
    ],
