      "Intervals: the busiest hour (half the morning trips, 10 % of the other trips: 0.3 by train, 0.2 by bus a resident and day) over places at 70 % (train 140, bus 49, tram 4.2 per m) at the rush-hour frequency × 1.5; the longest of 5, 10, 15, 20, 30, 60 min that is enough.",
      "The riders of a line for its interval: of the long ways of the morning (longer than walk_max_m) between stops of the line, the share the choice of the modes gives bus and tram for a way of that length (typicalShares: a car only to work, for those with a licence and a car; a bike for four in five where bikes are simulated); once the town has made 200 trips, 100 of them long, half of it what its people really took.",
      "Plans: work 06:30–08:00 until 15:30–17:30; school 07:00–07:40; shopping 08:30–11:30 and evenings; trains 05:45–07:45 and 16:00–18:30.",
      "Households (with together): per family one, two or three children (0.5, 0.37, 0.13) with two parents in 0.8 of them, else one; couples among 0.6 of the old and 0.5 of the other adults, the rest singles (Destatis 2023, rounded); a household has a car for each of its people who would have one, two at most.",
      "Going together: a child younger than 10 is taken to school by an adult of the household (one at home by day first, else one on the way to work or the train); the partner at home goes along shopping with 0.5 (old couples 0.7), a child at home with 0.5; pupils of a house to the same school walk in groups of two to four with 0.7. Who is led waits 25 clock minutes for the leader, then goes alone; a group that got apart at a stop waits 40 s for those still on their way.",
      "A group walks two abreast 0.7 m apart, the next row 0.9 m behind; in single file 0.8 m apart when the leader keeps to the right for somebody, waits or crosses a street; a child strays up to 0.6 m. People leave a building through its door one after the other, 1.1 s apart.",
      "A way up to walk_max_m is walked; for a longer one the person chooses. Bus or tram is an option where stops lie within 300 m of both ends and the connection (the walks, half the headway, the ride at 25 km/h) takes less than 1.3 × the walk; patience 20 clock minutes; a closed stop is not entered: walk instead, or away.",
      "From home, residents (not people from elsewhere: their car is elsewhere) have the car as an option with a driving licence while a car of the household stands there (a group: a driver among them, five people at most), and the bike if they have one (modes.bike.own; nobody with an aid, a pram or heavy or bulky luggage) where the cycling simulation runs and has a way for bikes, not as a group. A car or a bike left somewhere is taken on from there, and fetched before going home. To the train: on foot, by bus or tram, or by bike, never by car.",
      "Planned parts (simulated minutes): on foot at the person's (the group's) pace; bus or tram by its walks, half the headway and the ride; the car by the road traffic's planSeconds (without it 30 km/h on 1.3 × the straight line), 30 m to it and 60 m from it, loading and unloading (carLegTime), 60 s to park, 0.20 € a km; the bike by the cycling simulation's planSeconds at 16 km/h (children 0.75, old people 0.85 of it), 25 s each to unlock and to lock, 20 m to it and from it.",
      "Expected = planned × the town's ratio of the mode at this hour (the car: the mean of it and the traffic news, liveRatio) × the person's own ((n × ratio + hearsay) / (n + hearsay) after n trips by that mode on this way); the minutes that are what they are (locking, loading, parking) stay. With stretch, what is travelled (and what the drive costs) counts that many times as long in the choice, not the waiting, nor the walks to and from a stop.",
      "Cost (min) = walking × 1.6 × weather × person + waiting × 2 × weather × person + riding + driving + cycling × 1.3 + the fixed minutes + € / 0.20 + the mode's constant (on foot −30, bike 0, bus and tram 10, car −7) + the person's liking − 7 for the mode taken last on this way + 14 × how badly it went there; the bike also −ln(the weather's share of cyclists) / sharpness. p ∝ exp(−0.07 × cost).",
      "The tastes are fitted to MiD 2017 for somebody who has all four modes: of 100 trips of half a kilometre about 60 on foot, 13 by bike, 22 by car, 4 by bus or tram; of one and a half kilometres about 25, 22, 44 and 9; of three about 3, 23, 59 and 15 (tests/js/modes.test.js holds them to it).",
      "The weather and the person: a minute on foot or at a stop counts 1.3 in rain (1.6 in heavy rain), 1.3 in snowfall, 1.15 in frost or above 30 °C; on foot 1.1 in the dark, 1.15 on snow, 1.4 on ice; with a stick 1.4, a rollator 1.8, a wheelchair 1.5, a pram 1.2, heavy luggage 1.5, bulky 1.7, old people 1.2; for children and old people a minute on foot or on the bike in the dark counts 1.15 more (on the bike 1.15 in the dark for everybody).",
      "A trip went badly: by car a drive of jam (2) times its plan or more; by bus or tram left behind or given up waiting; on foot or by bike rain or snow at its end with more than 2 simulated minutes outside. The mood drops by 0.2; a good trip gives 0.03 back.",
      "The town's experience: 24 ratios per mode and kind of day (working days, weekends), cut to 0.5 … 6; hours nobody travelled in stay at 1. The town notes for the hour a trip began in: by bus and tram waiting, doors and riding against the planned wait and ride; the walk; the ride by bike; of the car the drive itself (the road traffic). An hour that is over moves its ratio by 0.35 × n / (n + 4) towards the mean of its n trips; while an hour runs, what was expected of it counts like 8 trips beside its trips so far.",
      "Shops are open 07:00–21:00; at most 30 people get off a train.",
      "Profiles from the stream of the world's seed and the person's id: the same person, the same profile; pupils (and pupils from elsewhere) are children, seniors old; trips of 30 km by train, 2 km in the town.",
      "A car or bike that is not drawn (no road traffic or cycling simulation, no way for it): the walks to and from it at the person's speed, loading and unloading, the drive at 30 km/h or the ride on 1.3 × the straight line, parking or locking; nothing is learned from it.",
      "Trips from door to door in clock minutes: on foot, waiting, at the doors, riding, by car, by bike; ended arrived, at the train, or otherwise; with the mode, whether it went badly and whether it was made with others; the latest 5000 kept for the statistics by group and the shares of the modes (modalSplit).",
